/* The image format table. Every per-format fact the HAL, Runtime, compiler and Python package use is a column
 * here; tools/generate_formats.py writes python/vernon_dsl/_formats.py from it and a test fails when that file
 * is stale.
 *
 * Define VERNON_FORMAT before including this file; it is undefined at the end.
 *
 * VERNON_FORMAT(name, NAME, texture, component_class, pixel_bytes, data_format, data_type, baseline,
 *               gl_internal_format, gl_format, gl_type, vulkan, dxgi, metal, spirv_storage)
 *
 *   name, NAME          Canonical manifest/Python name and the enumerator suffix of VernonTextureFormat.
 *   texture             Fixed ABI value of VERNON_TEXTURE_<NAME>.
 *   component_class     "float", "unorm", "snorm", "uint" or "sint"; the shader-visible result class.
 *   pixel_bytes         Bytes per texel; depth-stencil uploads use the packed 8-byte layout.
 *   data_format,        VERNON_HAL_IMAGE_DATA_<data_format> and VERNON_HAL_IMAGE_DATA_<data_type> of a whole-texel
 *   data_type           transfer. data_format DEPTH or DEPTH_STENCIL gives the depth and stencil aspects; any
 *                       other gives the color aspect.
 *   baseline            Space-separated capabilities the format class allows: renderable, blendable, filterable,
 *                       storage, resolvable, multisample and copyable. Devices only narrow this set.
 *   gl_*                OpenGL internal format, and the format and type of a whole-texel transfer; that pair also
 *                       allocates the image.
 *   vulkan, dxgi, metal Native formats; VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED, DXGI_FORMAT_UNKNOWN and MTLPixelFormatInvalid mark a
 *                       format the backend cannot create.
 *   spirv_storage       spirv::ImageFormat of a storage image; Unknown exactly when baseline lacks storage.
 *
 * Rows are only appended: texture values are ABI. */

VERNON_FORMAT(r8_unorm, R8_UNORM, 4, "unorm", 1, RED, UINT8,
              "renderable blendable filterable storage resolvable multisample copyable", 0x8229, 0x1903, 0x1401,
              VK_FORMAT_R8_UNORM, DXGI_FORMAT_R8_UNORM, MTLPixelFormatR8Unorm, R8)
